<p>Iran has installed a new supreme leader, Mojtaba Khamenei, as fighting spreads across the Middle East and Iran’s powerful Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) takes an increasingly central role in national-security decision-making. Several accounts say the IRGC pushed the succession through internal resistance, while the new leader has kept a low public profile since taking the post. The change at the top matters because the supreme leader’s office has grown into a dominant, security-focused institution that shapes Iran’s most sensitive files. It also matters because the IRGC answers directly to the supreme leader and helps set Iran’s military posture at home and abroad. With the transition unfolding during wartime, rhetoric has sharpened: President Trump demanded Iran’s “unconditional surrender,” and the IRGC said Iran was “fully prepared for a prolonged war,” highlighting how tightly leadership succession and conflict dynamics are now intertwined.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/D2J9S0tl6EOe1c6K3PRQnjOlPUQhCUJs-BnFw43K7eOiJ_wf5okAzYispV8Jy6fAi7B699JK-bPjB6vkoyHLgioQuEJ4BWu6KUP1yop_gLZfVSxpYBEGKs3WQbzInTS2K-vmqzLwZzEMUznNI9iBfQlGRM7GBdBu7cbHnEbKgYTgxj97f3rB3G60NqGeIjo7VD1fpnPEU2kMDck2' alt='Mojtaba Khamenei, son of the former supreme leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei, pictured in Tehran in 2019.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Why the IRGC backed him: Senior Iranian sources told Reuters the Guards saw Mojtaba Khamenei as a more pliant version of his father and expected him to support their hardline policies.</li><li>How opposition surfaced: Those sources said misgivings among senior political and clerical figures briefly slowed the process, pushing the public announcement back by hours.</li><li>War-driven leverage: Reuters’ account says the IRGC was already powerful but has gained even more sway since the war began, helping it override objections and steer the transition.</li><li>What analysts expect abroad: Coverage of the Reuters reporting says the IRGC believed Mojtaba Khamenei’s elevation could lead to a more aggressive stance outside Iran.</li><li>IRGC’s footprint: Primers describe the IRGC as a feared paramilitary force embedded across Iran’s political and security system, not just a conventional military actor.</li></ul><blockquote>I heard the news that Mr. Mojtaba Khamenei had been injured. I asked some friends with connections. They told me that, thank God, he is safe and sound. - Yousef Pezeshkian</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: President Trump demanded Iran’s “unconditional surrender,” a message reported in the context of the widening conflict. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/who-are-irans-revolutionary-guards/article70726242.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Senior Iranian sources (Reuters): They said the Revolutionary Guards forced through Mojtaba Khamenei’s selection over concerns from pragmatists and some clerical and political figures, reflecting the Guards’ leverage during wartime. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/irans-new-leader-still-silent-was-elevated-revolutionary-guards'>Al-Monitor (Reuters)</a>)</li><li>The New York Times: It describes the institution the new leader inherits as sprawling and secretive, noting it evolved from a more traditional religious-affairs operation into a national-security-centered power hub. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/10/world/middleeast/iran-supreme-leader-secretive-office.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/who-are-irans-revolutionary-guards/article70726242.ece'>Who are Iran’s Revolutionary Guards?</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/irans-new-leader-still-silent-was-elevated-by-the-revolutionary-guards'>Iran’s new leader, still silent, was elevated by the Revolutionary Guards</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/inside-irans-new-supreme-leader-mojtaba-khameneis-challenges-his-networks-and-arsenal-11198711#publisher=newsstand'>Inside Iran&#x27;s New Supreme Leader&#x27;s Challenges, His Networks And Arsenal</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/10/world/middleeast/iran-supreme-leader-secretive-office.html'>New Supreme Leader Inherits Sprawling, Secretive Office That Dominates Iran</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/war-middle-east-latest-developments-6'>War in the Middle East: latest developments</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-what-to-know-about-irans-islamic-revolutionary-guard-corps/'>What to know about Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li></ul>